# Espressif ESP32-family boards — hand the USB interfaces to the seat-local
# user, and keep ModemManager's hands off them. Same shape as
# 70-flipper-zero.rules; read that file's header for the reasoning behind
# uaccess over MODE="0666" and behind ID_MM_DEVICE_IGNORE.
#
# Matched on the whole Espressif vendor id (303a), not a PID list. The chips
# enumerate under several PIDs depending on chip and mode:
#   303a:1001  USB-Serial-JTAG on C3/S3/C6/H2 (the M32 Pocket shows up as this):
#              a CDC-ACM tty -> /dev/ttyACM*, plus a vendor-specific JTAG
#              interface that is NOT a tty, so `dialout` does nothing for it and
#              OpenOCD/WebUSB debugging is root-only without this rule
#   303a:0002  S2/S3 ROM download mode over native USB (TinyUSB CDC)
#   303a:80xx+ PIDs Espressif sublicenses to board makers running TinyUSB firmware
# A PID list would miss the next board. 303a is Espressif's own VID, so the
# wildcard only reaches ESP hardware, and uaccess never grants more than the
# seated user.
#
# Boards behind a CP210x/CH340 bridge (10c4/1a86) enumerate as the bridge, not
# as 303a, and are not covered here; they get a ttyUSB* that `dialout` handles.
#
# Numbered below 73 for the same reason as the Flipper rule: 73-seat-late.rules
# acts on the uaccess tag, and a higher number silently drops the ACL.
SUBSYSTEMS=="usb", ATTRS{idVendor}=="303a", TAG+="uaccess", ENV{ID_MM_DEVICE_IGNORE}="1"
